  "hooks": [
    "Lehi's three blessings are three arguments: a covenant land (1), opposition and choice (2), a latter-day seer (3).",
    "Nephi's psalm (4:16–35) is the one place he admits weakness at length — right after his father dies.",
    "Chapter 5 splits one family into the two nations the rest of the Book of Mormon is about.",
    "Nephi quotes Isaiah because his soul delights in his words (11:2), then explains him in plainness (25:4).",
    "It ends with doctrine, not history: faith, repentance, baptism, the Holy Ghost, endure (31)."
  ]
